  "term": "HR",
  "definition": "HR means heart rate. In this psychology context, short-term changes in heart rate are used to track how a person responds to stimuli, with brief slowing linked to orienting and attention to moderate or novel events, and speeding up linked to defensive responding to intense or aversive events.",
